   Anyway, I've just begun designing (not writing yet) a new game *based on*
Moria, Angband, NetHack, etc. It also takes a bit from the old Dungeon of
Doom. I've decided to call it "Dol Guldur", after the tower of the
Necromancer.

   Similar to Dungeon of Doom I'm using an iconic interface, rather than a
textual one. I'm programming on the Mac, currently in Modula-2 or Pascal as
I don't *yet* know C ...

   Anyway, I want help/ I've only played Moria, but I've got the general
idea. I want suggestions for monsters, items, traps, etc. Not only do I
want statistics for these things, but I want *icons*. Monochrome only as
I don't have a colour machine.

   I intend to have about 20 tower levels, followed by a dungeon of about
50 levels which can only be reached through the top of the tower :) The
final monster is Sauron (who, BTW cannot be killed, merely dispelled ...
I'm paving the way already for a sequel ... "Barad Dur", the Black Tower).

   I've got the wall, floor and door icons. Anything would need to fit
*inside* my floor icons (there are two). I'll include the two icons here
in Hexadecimal so anyone designing icons for me (hint hint ...) can fit
them. Simply make sure there is enough white space around your icon so it
will fit both floor icons.

   If you do decide to submit something, please include an icon for it. I am
